      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Under CIF Incoterms 2020, while the seller must obtain insurance, they are only required to provide minimum coverage equivalent to Institute Cargo Clauses (C) or similar minimum terms, which exclude total loss or damage due to fire and other specified perils. The contract explicitly states that this insertion does not extend the prevailing rules regarding the minimum coverage to the maximum (ICC A), meaning the seller is providing the bare statutory minimum unless otherwise agreed. Consequently, advising the buyer to verify if this limited coverage aligns with their actual commercial risk exposure and whether stricter indemnification is needed.",
